-- The first-call backlog is not trimmed to "from now"; the cap bounds it.
-- A long quiet spell piles the inbox up as raw lines. Measured 2026-11-09: `voice-app.jsonl` held 668 lines since October, about 261 unread; 369 began "done:" (finished agents re-reporting "nothing running") and 188 were raw `follow` deltas. Proposed fix, in order: (1) `updates` returns a digest by default (one line per sender: its latest message and a count), raw lines behind a flag; (2) on resume, show "newest per sender since the cursor" and say how many lines were skipped; (3) stop the duplicate "done, idle" messages at the sender (an open item in [ai/handover.md](/framework/ai/handover.md)) and do not auto-follow `page.jsonl` / `session.jsonl` into the inbox. Big-picture state belongs in the session logs, not the inbox.
